# {{title}} component

A Zeyn component crate: one component with a browser script, a stylesheet and texts of its own,
shipped the way the framework ships its own components. `zeyn mcp` serves the framework rules as
the `zeyn_docs` topic `rules`, and `.claude/skills/zeyn/SKILL.md` has the language in short.
Extra rules for a component crate:

1. The crate is `{{name}}`, its browser module is `{{component}}`. Classes start with
   `z-{{component}}-`, attributes with `data-zeyn-{{component}}-` and text keys with
   `{{component}}.`. `App::module` stops the app at startup when a name breaks this.
2. A page links the module only when its HTML holds a marker (`module()` in `src/lib.rs`), and
   `zeyn.js` loads it when such content arrives later. `tests/{{component}}.rs` checks that a
   page without the component never references the module; keep that test passing.
3. The stylesheet takes colors and sizes from theme tokens (`var(--z-text)`, `var(--z-space)`)
   and never from literal colors, so the light and the dark theme both work. Keep focus visible
   and the component usable with the keyboard (W3C APG pattern for the widget).
4. The script is an ES module without inline handlers; the Content Security Policy stays strict.
   Content that arrives later reaches it through the `zeyn:content` event, or through one
   listener on the document.
5. Every user facing text goes into `assets/*.json` (the component) or `locales/*.json` (the example), with the same keys in each locale
   file (`cargo test` checks the component). An app can reword any text in its own catalogs.
6. The component works in an app of the same Zeyn version only. Release by tagging
   (`git tag v0.2.0 && git push --tags`) and raise the minor version for a breaking change.
7. A source file holds at most 300 non blank lines (`build.rs`) and a function at most 60 lines
   (clippy `too_many_lines`).

Run the example with `cargo run --example demo` (http://127.0.0.1:3011): the start page holds no
component and links no module, the second page holds one.

